                     <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card provides the
                        following context for the rejection:</p><p>
                        <q>M. R. James (1895) says <q>Provenance: Durham (?)</q>. But on fol. 148 is
                           a letter of William bishop of Norwich [...] [see above], and in between
                           fols. 80 and 81 is stitched a document of <persName>Oliver
                              Sutton</persName>, bishop of Lincoln 1280-99, mentioning a rector of
                           Haverhill (Essex).</q></p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Top of fol. 106r: <q>Liber magistri <persName
